      "title": "Scientists trick cancer cells into making the drugs that kill them",
      "description": "Scientists have developed a promising new cancer-fighting strategy that uses carbon monoxide naturally produced by tumor cells to manufacture powerful drugs inside the cancer cells themselves. Early laboratory experiments suggest the technique could selectively attack cancer while sparing healthy cells, potentially paving the way for safer chemotherapy alternatives.",
      "link": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261101010552.htm",
